  "verbalization": "Doxacurium Chloride appears to interact with Chrnb1 through a shared pathway involving organonitrogen compounds. The evidence suggests that Doxacurium Chloride binds to Chrna2, which is then bound by Tubocurarine or Vecuronium, both of which in turn bind to Chrnb1. The lowest common ancestor of these interactions is the organonitrogen compound, indicating a common biochemical mechanism. This suggests that Doxacurium Chloride may act through a similar mechanism as other compounds that bind to Chrna2 and subsequently to Chrnb1, potentially through a shared receptor or signaling pathway. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Doxacurium Chloride and Chrnb1 via a chain of binding events involving organonitrogen compounds, highlighting a possible role in modulating receptor activity or signaling.",
